# asave's modes (olc_save.c do_asave), with a builder (Planner, security 9) and a mortal (Delver, security 0).
# Areas are numbered in load order: 0 is immort.are, 2 shire.are, 3 midgaard.are.
# - Delver: asave 2 is refused; asave world saves only area.lst (every area is refused quietly), so shire.are is
#   still the stock file; asave list rewrites area.lst for anyone
# - a mob: asave area does nothing without a connection; asave 2 is refused (a mob is never a builder)
# - Planner: no argument and an unknown word give the syntax; 999 is no area; 0 and 2 save those areas;
#   changed saves nothing (no area has changed) and says None.; area needs an editor
@connect d
Delver
psswrd
@return
asave 2
asave world
@file shire.are
@file area.lst
asave list
@connect b
Planner
smoke123
@return
@return
goto 3001
force hassan asave area
force hassan asave 2
asave
asave nonsense
asave 999
asave -1
asave 0
@file immort.are
asave 2
@file shire.are
asave changed
asave area
asave  world
asave WORLD
@file midgaard.are
